fact WorkItem(id: "WI-139", description: some(value: "Disable automatic application of equational rewrite rules to Z3 emission. Equational laws like add_comm: 'add(a, b) = add(b, a)' inside Numeric / Ring / VectorSpace specs become forall-quantified Z3 axioms when emitted, which can blow up quantifier instantiation (commutativity rewrites loop in E-matching, distributivity multiplies term count). User concern: such laws should NOT be ambient axioms; they should require explicit 'using <law-name>' to be visible to the SMT discharge. Approach options: (a) add a [rewrite: false] meta annotation on rule blocks; (b) treat equational rules (head ?= body shape) as Pending until cited via using; (c) split the spec into 'operations' and 'lemmas' sections where lemmas are off-by-default. Acceptance: cargo-test passes; lf1 still discharges 12/12; the new Ring/VectorSpace law rules don't appear in the Z3 document for lf1 obligations unless explicitly cited."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-04-28T17:30:46Z"))
